ecause he  jeweled Grindelwald inside of the London  Underground with spells blasting all  over the place it doesn't sound entirely  outside the realm of possibility for a  spell to have bounced off of a wall map  becoming somewhat infused with the  pattern and subsequently permeating  itself into Dumbledore's skin spells in  Harry Potter have historically exhibited  all sorts of strange properties and this  seems like just the kind of strange but  oddly significant thing that could  happen to someone like Dumbledore  the only problem with this theory is  that the latest Fantastic Beasts films  seem to predominantly take place in  countries beside Britain and I've always  been of the impression that their final  Jewel took place on grindelwald's home  turf this is reinforced by the fact that  Grindelwald ended up being imprisoned in  nermanguard rather than Azkaban  furthermore if this was indeed how he  got the scar why would this scenario  cause Dumbledore to be fond of it given  how close Grindelwald and Dumbledore  were you'd imagine that a scar reminding  him of their battle with illicit bad  memories but here's the thing defeating  Grindelwald wasn't all bad by defeating  Grindelwald Albus Dumbledore helped Save  The Wizarding World and many many lives  he put others first and himself second  yes he had to fight the man that he once  loved but in one Fell Swoop he was able  to both save the day and keep  Grindelwald alive grindelwald's defeat  also represented a shift in his  perspective after being finally defeated  by Dumbledore he inevitably came to the  realization that he had always been  wrong and this is reflected by the fact  that he never even tried to escape  nerman God he knew that he got what he  deserved and that he would need to pay  his Penance Zing Grindelwald like that  must have brought Dumbledore great joy  despite the length that he had to go to  prompt this realization and that's it  for this video if you enjoy the content  please be sure 